    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60-a1">

                <pb facs="0118" n="772" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg772"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 84.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Admiral Reynolds to
                        Mr. Cadwalader.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-11-05"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 5,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department is gratified to receive your
                    letter of the 3d instant and its inclosures.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to request that you will convey to the authorities of Japan the
                    thanks of the Department for the facilities extended Professor Davidson, United
                    States Navy, and his associates, to enable them properly to observe the transit
                    of Venus; also to Mr. Bingham for his prompt action in the matter.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant.</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. REYNOLDS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of the
                            Navy</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Honorable <hi rendition="#small-caps">John L. Cadwalader</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
